      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transportation In Nichlaul Maharajganj</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
   <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Daylight condition re-inspection against pickup photos: The consignee and delivery representative conduct a thorough exterior and interior examination under natural daylight to maximize visibility and eliminate shadow-induced distortions. Each panel, glass surface, tire, and trim component is systematically compared against the high-resolution photographic evidence captured during pickup. Any discrepancies, scratches, dents, or pre-existing anomalies are documented immediately, ensuring that transit-related damages are clearly distinguished from origin conditions.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Odometer verification against the LR bilty: The current mileage reading is recorded directly from the vehicle dashboard and cross-referenced with the declared figures on the Logistics Receipt bilty. This step confirms that the vehicle was not operated beyond authorized transit limits, prevents unauthorized usage during cargo handling, and validates contractual distance allowances. Any variance exceeding the agreed tolerance threshold triggers an immediate investigation before acceptance proceeds.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Signed condition sign-off: Once visual and mechanical verifications align with the original documentation, both parties review the final inspection checklist. The consignee acknowledges receipt by affixing a wet signature and timestamp to the delivery manifest, while the carrier representative countersigns to confirm procedural compliance. This legally binding document serves as conclusive proof of successful handover, closes the liability window, and updates the shipment status in the tracking system.</span></li>
   </ul>
   <p>Executing this standardized handover framework minimizes post-delivery claims, strengthens audit trails, and reinforces trust across the automotive logistics network. Adherence to daylight validation, mileage reconciliation, and authenticated sign-off ensures every vehicle transition meets industry-grade accountability standards.</p></div>
